 R←Test_UC_031(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;newFolder;rc;msg;result;stop
⍝ Runs ]Status with and without -allUntracked on a project that has a folder which is entirely
⍝ new. Git names such a folder but not the files within it, which is what made <CompareCommits>
⍝ miss them when comparing the working area with the last commit.\\
⍝ Works on a private copy of the fixture because it adds a folder to the project.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed
 stop←0

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 newFolder←tempDir,'/APLSource/NewStuff'
 ⎕MKDIR newFolder
 (⊂' r←New' ' r←42')⎕NPUT(newFolder,'/New.aplf')1

 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'Status "',tempDir,'" -noAPLnames'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂'APLSource/NewStuff/')∊result[;3]        ⍝ The folder, and nothing within it

 (rc msg result)←stop ∆UCMD'Status "',tempDir,'" -noAPLnames -allUntracked'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp~(⊂'APLSource/NewStuff/New.aplf')∊result[;3]
 →T.GoToTidyUp(⊂'APLSource/NewStuff/')∊result[;3]         ⍝ Now the folder itself is not reported

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
